  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1132 PM CDT WED SEP 2 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will remain steadfast to start this forecast\nperiod, as the center of it remains just to our north. This\nridge, and in turn the heat, will remain the main weather story\nfor most of the next week, as afternoon highs will continue to\nclimb into the mid and upper-90s. Heat index values will remain\nabove Heat Advisory criteria during this time, with peak\nafternoon numbers ranging between 105 and 108 degrees. The\nexisting Heat Advisory remains in effect until 8 PM Saturday. The\nridge will slightly break down into the weekend, allowing for a\nweak disturbance to move in from the Gulf. This should increase\nrain chances for a portion of the forecast area, but confidence\nhere is low regarding the overall impact to heat index values.\n\nBy Sunday, the center of the ridge will slide to the west,\nallowing for at least low-end (20-30%) rain chances to return to\nthe forecast. These rain chances will unfortunately be short\nlived, as a deep trough begins to take shape over the west coast\ncome Tuesday. This trough will push the apex of the ridge back\neast, returning it to a location similar to where it currently\nresides. Afternoon highs should quickly rebound in this scenario,\nwith additional periods of heat headlines running into next\nweekend.\n\n/44/",
